 \section{Discussion}
 
+\subsection{Contribution beyond the known risk}
+
+SWAN already anticipates multi-sentence attacks, and AliMark and SwordStamp
+already analyze and mitigate structural perturbations. The paper's focus
+is therefore the evidence added by a reproducible case study, an explicit
+optimization contract, and a system audit. The A--B--A result measures a
+specific reversible behavior; its statistical explanation is elementary.
+The DP supplies a complete minimum for stated local detector classes; its
+proof uses standard principles. The resource study distinguishes a healthy
+detector from an executable certificate on the frozen workload.
+
+These contributions remain limited. The available behavior does not
+establish an AMR-specific mechanism at normal length, and the exact
+framework has no final real certified rate. The work should be assessed
+as a bounded audit and exact-evaluation study, rather than as a new
+watermark, a previously unknown attack class, or a general impossibility
+theorem. The number of engineering iterations is not itself evidence of
+novelty.
+
